# Final paycheck deadline — Acme Cloud Systems (US)

> Module Final_paycheck_acme
> Using Legal_types as T

Sources: SYN-005 § 9.3–9.4 (handbook) as the base, displaced by REAL-003
(Cal. Lab. Code § 201), REAL-004 (§ 202), REAL-005 (§ 227.3) and REAL-002
(C.R.S. § 8-4-109). The handbook again supplies the authority:

  SYN-005 § 9.5 — Where applicable state law requires final wages to be paid earlier than
  the next regular payroll date, Payroll will issue final wages by the deadline that law
  requires.

Catala dates carry no time of day, so § 202's "within 72 hours" is encoded as three days.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FinalPaycheck:
  input last_day content date
  input separation content T.Separation
  input work_state content T.WorkState
  input next_regular_payroll_date content date

  output due_date content date
  output pto_payout_required content boolean
```

## SYN-005 § 9.3–9.4 — the handbook's base rule

  Final wages, including any earned and unpaid incentive compensation, are paid on the
  next regular payroll date following the employee's last day of employment. […] Accrued
  unused PTO is not paid out on separation, except where applicable state law requires
  payout.

```catala
scope FinalPaycheck:
  label handbook_9_3
  definition due_date equals next_regular_payroll_date

  label handbook_9_4
  definition pto_payout_required equals false
```

## REAL-003, Cal. Lab. Code § 201(a) — discharge

  If an employer discharges an employee, the wages earned and unpaid at the time of
  discharge are due and payable immediately.

```catala
scope FinalPaycheck:
  exception handbook_9_3
  definition due_date
    under condition
      work_state = T.WorkState.CA
      and separation = T.Separation.InvoluntaryTermination
    consequence equals last_day
```

## REAL-004, Cal. Lab. Code § 202(a) — quitting

  If an employee not having a written contract for a definite period quits his or her
  employment, his or her wages shall become due and payable not later than 72 hours
  thereafter, unless the employee has given 72 hours previous notice of his or her
  intention to quit, in which case the employee is entitled to his or her wages at the
  time of quitting.

```catala
scope FinalPaycheck:
  exception handbook_9_3
  definition due_date
    under condition
      work_state = T.WorkState.CA
      and separation = T.Separation.QuitWithoutNotice
    consequence equals last_day + 3 day

  exception handbook_9_3
  definition due_date
    under condition
      work_state = T.WorkState.CA
      and separation = T.Separation.QuitWithNotice
    consequence equals last_day
```

## REAL-002, C.R.S. § 8-4-109(1)(a) — Colorado discharge

Wages are due immediately on an involuntary termination; where the payroll unit is not
operating at that moment the statute allows a short grace period, which is not encoded
because Acme's payroll unit runs daily.

```catala
scope FinalPaycheck:
  exception handbook_9_3
  definition due_date
    under condition
      work_state = T.WorkState.CO
      and separation = T.Separation.InvoluntaryTermination
    consequence equals last_day
```

## REAL-005, Cal. Lab. Code § 227.3 — vacation is wages

  Whenever a contract of employment or employer policy provides for paid vacations, and an
  employee is terminated without having taken off his vested vacation time, all vested
  vacation shall be paid to him as wages at his final rate.

Colorado treats earned vacation the same way under C.R.S. § 8-4-101(14).

```catala
scope FinalPaycheck:
  exception handbook_9_4
  definition pto_payout_required
    under condition
      work_state = T.WorkState.CA or work_state = T.WorkState.CO
    consequence equals true
```
